        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0208" n="120" xml:id="pg120"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received August 9.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1544.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my dispatch No. 1542 of June 17, I
                    transmitted to you copies of a correspondence between the foreign office and
                    myself touching the question whether the President had approved the recent act
                    of Congress relating to Chinese restriction. Having received your cablegram of
                    June 17, of which I acknowledged the receipt in my dispatch No. 1543 of June 19,
                    I sent this day to the foreign office a communication of which a copy is
                    herewith inclosed. I shall await your instructions of the 17th ultimo before
                    taking any further action.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d90-a1.xml" xpointer="d90-a1"/>
